<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE-MARANDA Q2 NET UP, MULLS RIGHTS ISSUE.</title>
<headline>TABLE-MARANDA Q2 NET UP, MULLS RIGHTS ISSUE.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net income before capital spending</p>
<p>					  5.45  vs 3.86</p>
<p>    Capital spending		0.61  vs 1.14</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled		 23,239  vs 22,601</p>
<p>Metal in concentrate sold</p>
<p>    - zinc sales (tonnes)	3,197  vs 3,425</p>
<p>    - copper sales (tonnes)    431    vs 421</p>
<p>Full name: Maranda Mines Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that an 18 cents dividend would be paid around August 29 to members registered on August 22.</p>
<p>The group recently announced that a consortium in which it owns a 30 percent stake had been awarded the tender by Zambia Consolidated Copper Mines to buy the Chibuluma Mine.</p>
<p>It said the purchase consideration and capital expenditure financing was expected to take the form of debt and equity finance in a Zambian registered company which is to be formed.</p>
<p>On completion of the debt financing arrangements, the equity finance required by Maranda is envisaged by means of a rights issue.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
